{
 "_about": "What random talismans (melded charms) can roll, from the game data (dtlnor/MHWs-in-json RandomAmulet* tables). Skill slot 1 draws from the primary pool (weapon-kind skills, 1-4 points), skill slots 2-3 from the secondary pool (armor-kind skills, 5-10 points, 0 = empty). Decoration slots: weapon-kind slot = ACC_TYPE_00, armor-kind slot = ACC_TYPE_01. A talisman rolls one of point_rows for its rarity, then for each skill point value a lot_skills entry worth exactly that many points (1-4 points = weapon-kind table, 5-10 = armor-kind table, 0 = empty) and the slot pattern worth slot_points. Used for validating user-entered talismans and for the \"every possible talisman\" mode. Rarities are the ones the game shows (the RARE enum of the dump is one lower): 5 Unknown, 6 Historical, 7 Secret, 8 Golden Age Charm (the only one with a weapon slot).",
